348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 268 0 R
/T (Air pressure P pushes on the cavity wall. Because the cavity sits 3 mm off-centre, the wall on one side is thin \(3 mm\) and on the other thick \(9 mm\). The thin side stretches more, so the tube curls towards the thick side. The question is how far the tip moves for a given pressure, and which model predicts it reliably.)
/E (Air pressure P pushes on the cavity wall. Because the cavity sits 3 mm off-centre, the wall on one side is thin \(3 mm\) and on the other thick \(9 mm\). The thin side stretches more, so the tube curls towards the thick side. The question is how far the tip moves for a given pressure, and which model predicts it reliably.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
